#: translations.php:5
msgid ""
"The first step in creating a national or diocesan calendar, is to translate "
"the data for the General Roman Calendar into the language for that nation or "
"diocese."
msgstr ""
"Primus gradus in creando calendarium nationale vel diœcesanum est data pro "
"Calendario Generali Romano in linguam illius nationis vel diœcesis "
"transferre."

#: translations.php:9
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This can be done on the <a href=\"%1$s\" target=\"_blank\">LitCal "
"translation server %2$s</a>."
msgstr ""
"Hoc fieri potest in <a href=\"%1$s\" target=\"_blank\">LitCal translationis "
"servo %2$s</a>."

#: translations.php:14
msgid ""
"If you would like to contribute to the translations of the Liturgical data "
"for your region, please feel free to create an account on the translation "
"server."
msgstr ""
"Si vis conferre ad translationes notitiarum Liturgicarum pro tua regione, "
"libenter crea rationem in servo translationis."

#: translations.php:16
msgid "Specifically, the components which require translation are:"
msgstr "Speciatim, componentia quæ translationem requirunt sunt:"

#. translators: 1 = name of the translation component ("API strings"),
#. 2 = names of the categories, 3 = name of a category ("Calendar messages")
#: translations.php:20
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Other translations required for the Liturgical Calendar data are found in "
"the %1$s translation component. Upon choosing the language in which to "
"translate this component, you will find tags that categorize the strings for "
"translation in the \"String status\" section. The categories that are "
"required to complete the Liturgical calendar data are: %2$s. The %3$s tag / "
"category are the messages that explain how the calendar was calculated for a "
"given year; though not essential for the Calendar data, it is useful "
"information for understanding where the results of the current calculation "
"came from."
msgstr ""
"Aliæ translationes necessariæ ad data Calendarii Liturgici reperiuntur in "
"parte translationis %1$s. Cuma linguam elegeris in qua hæc pars vertenda "
"est, indices invenies qui series vertendas in sectione \"Status Serierum\" "
"categorizant. Categoriæ quæ ad data Calendarii Liturgici perficienda "
"requiruntur sunt: %2$s. Index vel categoria %3$s nuntios continet qui "
"explicant quomodo calendarium pro anno dato computatum sit; quamvis ad data "
"Calendarii non prorsus necessaria, est informatio utilis ad intellegendum "
"unde eventus computationis præsentis orti sint."

#: translations.php:49
#, php-format
msgid ""
"If translating liturgical calendar data for a European country, you will "
"also want to translate the %1$s component."
msgstr ""
"Si data calendarii liturgici pro natione Europæa vertis, etiam componentem "
"%1$s vertere vis."

#: translations.php:54
msgid ""
"Translations of the above mentioned liturgical events MUST NOT be done "
"simply based on the linguistic abilities of the translator, but MUST be "
"taken from the Roman Missal used in the region for which the translation is "
"accomplished."
msgstr ""
"Translationes eventuum liturgicorum supradictorum NON simpliciter ex "
"facultatibus linguisticis interpretis fieri debent, sed ex Missali Romano in "
"regione ad quam translatio perficitur sumendæ sunt."

#: translations.php:55
msgid ""
"Translations of the above mentioned liturgical events may change from one "
"edition of the Roman Missal to the next; translators should simply use the "
"most recent edition of the Roman Missal for their region as a reference."
msgstr ""
"Translationes eventuum liturgicorum supradictorum possunt mutari ab una "
"editione Missalis Romani ad aliam; interpretes simpliciter debent uti "
"recentissima editione Missalis Romani regionis suæ tamquam norma."

#: translations.php:56
msgid ""
"This API intends to be historically correct as regards the calculation of "
"the dates and the precedence of the liturgical events, but does not pretend "
"historical accuracy as regards differences in the translations of the "
"liturgical events over time."
msgstr ""
"Hæc API intendit historice recta esse quoad computationem dierum et "
"præcedentiam festorum, sed non prætendit historicæ accuratæ esse quoad "
"differentias in translationibus eventuum liturgicorum per tempora."

#: translations.php:58
msgid ""
"National calendars and related translations must be defined using data from "
"the translation of the Roman Missal used in the Region or in any case from "
"decrees of the Episcopal Conference of the Region."
msgstr ""
"Calendaria Nationalia et translationes pertinentes definiri debent ex data "
"translationis Missalis Romani in Regione usi vel quovis modo ex decretis "
"Conferentiæ Episcopalis Regionis."

#: translations.php:59
msgid ""
"Anyone who intends on contributing to the translations is required to agree "
"to these conditions."
msgstr ""
"Quicumque intendit ad translationes conferre, his condicionibus consentire "
"debet."

#: translations.php:60
msgid ""
"If the translator is not an expert in liturgical science or does not have a "
"role in a diocesan office for liturgy and worship, the translations will "
"require overview by a liturgical expert before being incorporated into this "
"project."
msgstr ""
"Si interpres non est peritus in scientia liturgica aut munus in officio "
"diœcesano pro liturgia et cultu non habet, translationes requirebunt "
"recognitionem a perito liturgico antequam in hoc proiecto incorporentur."

#: translations.php:67
msgid ""
"The project website can also be translated into other languages. The "
"translation strings can be found in the following translation components:"
msgstr ""
"Situs proiecti etiam in alias linguas verti potest. Filum translationis in "
"sequentibus componentibus translationis inveniri potest:"

